{
  "title": "Pathologic Scoliosis",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/spine/2059/pathologic-scoliosis",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 24 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathologic Scoliosis is a form of scoliosis resulting from a benign bone tumor most commonly located in the posterior elements of the spine.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with full-length standing spine radiographs to determine the severity of the curve. A CT scan is useful to assess for the size and location of the underlying lesion.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is observation and NSAIDs for small and minimally symptomatic curves. Surgical resection of the lesion is indicated for painful, progressive scoliosis.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "can occur in all age groups",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Causes",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**osteoid osteomas**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**occur in the apex of the concavity of the curve**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/2059/images/osteoid%20osteoma.jpg",
                      "caption": "osteoid osteoma"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "curves are typically rigid",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "can occur in the vertebral body or posterior elements",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "demonstrate same histology as osteoid osteomas in the peripheral skeleton",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**osteoblastomas**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "larger lesion than osteoid osteoma",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "pain is usually less severe than osteoid osteoma",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Mechanism",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "scoliosis is thought to develop in response to painful paraspinal muscle spasms",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "back pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "most commonly at night",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pain relieved by anti-inflammatories",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "less relief reported with osteoblastomas",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "posterior trunk",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "curvature of the spine",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "usually mild",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "neurological exam",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "may have neurological deficits with osteoblastoma",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "findings dependent on level of lesion",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "AP/Lateral of spine",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/2059/images/patho%20scoli%20ap.jpg",
                  "caption": "osteoid osteoma"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "can determine level and severity of curvature",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "lesion is defined by cortical thickening with radiolucent nidus",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "osteoid osteoma is less than 2 cm in diameter by definition",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "osteoblastoma is greater than 2 cm",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT scan",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/2059/images/scoli%20axial.jpg",
              "caption": "Osteoid osteoma of spine"
            },
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/2059/images/osteoid%20osteoma.jpg",
              "caption": "osteoid osteoma"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "fine cut best for outlining lesion and determining treatment plan",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "good for showing proximity to neurovascular structures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "may only show soft tissue edema and not the nidus",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Bone scan",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "markedly increased uptake in area of lesion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Non-operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "NSAIDs, observation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "minimal curve",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "may take up to 36 months to resolve",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "osteoblatomas usually do not respond to NSAIDS",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "en bloc resection of lesion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**painful, progressive scoliosis**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "resolution of curve if removed with 15-18 months of onset of curve in child less than 11 years old",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "radiofrequency ablation of lesion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "usually not an option due to proximity of neurological structures of spine",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "case by case basis based on 3D studies (CT, MRI)",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Outcomes good with treatment",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most cases of scoliosis due to osteoid osteoma will resolve after resection of tumor if",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "performed within 15-18 months of onset of curvature",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "child is less than 11 years of age",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
